Authorize isolated adapter profiles and configure local MCP clients

Usage:
  mcp-runtime adapter profile [command]

Available Commands:
  add           Create a profile using the selected platform login and an authorized session
  authorize     Explicitly authorize a session with the selected platform login
  client-config Write a local MCP client config including its credential to an owner-only file
  remove        Remove a profile and its stored credentials

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for profile

Global Flags:
      --debug              Enable debug mode with structured error logging
      --state-dir string   Owner-only adapter state directory (default "~/.mcpruntime/adapter")

Use "mcp-runtime adapter profile [command] --help" for more information about a command.
